---
import Sources from '../../components/Sources.astro';
import CarouselPlayground from '../../islands/CarouselPlayground.tsx';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const tones = ['primary', 'secondary', 'tertiary', 'error'];
/** A placeholder picture: a two-tone panel with its number (the docs have no photos). */
const tile = (i: number) =>
  `<div class="docs-carousel-tile" data-tone="${tones[i % tones.length]}"><span class="docs-carousel-tile__label">${String(i + 1)}</span></div>`;
const items = (count: number, attrs: (i: number) => string = () => '') =>
  Array.from(
    { length: count },
    (_, i) => `<m3e-carousel-item${attrs(i)}>${tile(i)}</m3e-carousel-item>`,
  ).join('');
const cssItems = (count: number) =>
  Array.from(
    { length: count },
    (_, i) =>
      `<div class="m3e-carousel__item" role="group" aria-roledescription="slide" aria-label="${String(i + 1)} of ${String(count)}" tabindex="0"><div class="m3e-carousel__mask">${tile(i)}</div></div>`,
  ).join('');
---

<Base title="Carousel">
  <h1>Carousel</h1>
  <p>
    A carousel (COMPONENT_SPEC §36) shows a row of visual items that scroll horizontally. As an item scrolls, its visible part grows and shrinks between the large, medium and small sizes and the items stay pinned together: the keylines of Compose's carousels, ported from <code>androidx.compose.material3.carousel</code> (the <code>Arrangement</code>, <code>Keylines</code>, <code>Strategy</code> and snap position math in m3e-motion). Items are masked with extra-large (28dp) corners. Scrolling is the browser's, with native snapping: one item at a time for the multi-browse and hero layouts, free for the uncontained layout.
  </p>
  <p>
    Keyboard: every item is a tab stop, and the arrow keys also move between items (Home and End to the ends); a focused item scrolls to its place. Items are APG slides ("2 of 5") in a region with the carousel role description; give the carousel a name. With reduced motion, items keep one size and are not masked. Compose's defaults put no space between items and no padding at the ends (<code>CarouselDefaults</code>); the examples here use the 8dp spacing and 16dp padding of the Compose samples and m3.material.io specs (<code>item-spacing</code>, <code>content-padding</code>).
  </p>

  <section aria-labelledby="multi-browse-heading">
    <h2 id="multi-browse-heading">Multi-browse (element)</h2>
    <p>
      <code>&lt;m3e-carousel layout="multi-browse" item-width="186"&gt;</code> fits large, medium and small items into the width, changing the large size as little as possible (here 412dp wide, as the Compose sample: two 178dp items, a 40dp one). Small items are 40–56dp. The <strong>Show all</strong> button is the m3.material.io way to reach every item without scrolling sideways.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-carousel-frame">
      <m3e-carousel label="Featured" item-width="186" item-spacing="8" content-padding="16" data-testid="multi-browse">
        <Fragment set:html={items(8)} />
      </m3e-carousel>
      <div class="docs-carousel-show-all">
        <button type="button" class="m3e-button m3e-button--text">Show all</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Interactive items</h3>
    <p>
      <code>href</code> makes an item a link and <code>action</code> a button (activating it fires <code>action</code> with <code>&#123; index &#125;</code> from the item, bubbling through the carousel; the carousel's <code>item-click</code> is deprecated since 1.8 and removed in 2.0): the item then shows the state layer and ripple over its content. Static items take the focus themselves.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-carousel-frame">
      <m3e-carousel label="Albums" item-width="186" item-spacing="8" content-padding="16" data-testid="interactive">
        <Fragment set:html={items(6, (i) => (i % 2 === 0 ? ` href="#carousel-item-${String(i + 1)}"` : ' action'))} />
      </m3e-carousel>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="uncontained-heading">
    <h2 id="uncontained-heading">Uncontained (element)</h2>
    <p>
      <code>layout="uncontained" item-width="186"</code>: items keep their width and the last visible one is cut off at the edge, shrinking as it leaves. It does not snap.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-carousel-frame">
      <m3e-carousel layout="uncontained" label="Recent" item-width="186" item-spacing="8" content-padding="16" data-testid="uncontained">
        <Fragment set:html={items(8)} />
      </m3e-carousel>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
    <h2 id="hero-heading">Hero (element)</h2>
    <p>
      <code>layout="hero"</code>: one large item and a small one after it. Without <code>item-width</code> the large item fills the width but for the small item; with it, more large items fit. One item per swipe.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-carousel-frame">
      <m3e-carousel layout="hero" label="Spotlight" item-spacing="8" content-padding="16" data-testid="hero">
        <Fragment set:html={items(6)} />
      </m3e-carousel>
    </div>

    <h3>Center-aligned hero</h3>
    <p>
      <code>layout="centered-hero"</code> (Compose's <code>HorizontalCenteredHeroCarousel</code>): the large item between two small ones; the first and last items align with the edges instead. Fewer than three items stay start-aligned.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-carousel-frame docs-carousel-frame--inset">
      <m3e-carousel layout="centered-hero" label="Highlights" item-spacing="8" content-padding="16" data-testid="centered-hero">
        <Fragment set:html={items(6)} />
      </m3e-carousel>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="full-screen-heading">
    <h2 id="full-screen-heading">Full screen (CSS)</h2>
    <p>
      <code>layout="full-screen"</code>: one item fills the carousel and the items scroll vertically, 16dp apart, snapping to each one (m3.material.io; Compose has no full-screen carousel). Give the carousel a height (here 360dp); ArrowUp and ArrowDown move between items.
    </p>
    <div class="docs-carousel-full-screen">
      <m3e-carousel layout="full-screen" label="Stories" data-testid="full-screen">
        <Fragment set:html={items(4)} />
      </m3e-carousel>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="css-heading">
    <h2 id="css-heading">Without JavaScript (CSS)</h2>
    <p>
      The m3e-css markup alone scrolls and snaps items at <code>--m3e-comp-carousel-item-width</code>, without the keyline sizes or masks (the same layout reduced motion shows).
    </p>
    <div class="docs-carousel-frame">
      <div class="m3e-carousel m3e-carousel--multi-browse" role="region" aria-roledescription="carousel" aria-label="Static" style="--m3e-comp-carousel-item-width: 186px; --m3e-comp-carousel-item-spacing: 8px; --m3e-comp-carousel-content-padding-start: 16px; --m3e-comp-carousel-content-padding-end: 16px" data-testid="css-only">
        <div class="m3e-carousel__viewport" tabindex="-1"><Fragment set:html={cssItems(6)} /></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="react-heading">
    <h2 id="react-heading">React</h2>
    <p>
      <code>&lt;Carousel layout itemWidth itemSpacing contentPadding aria-label&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;CarouselItem href onPress&gt;</code> children renders the same DOM as the element; its ref has <code>scrollToItem(index)</code> and <code>currentItem</code>.
    </p>
    <CarouselPlayground client:only="react" />
  </section>

  <Sources>
    <p>
      androidx Compose Material3 1.5.0-beta01 (<code>19991f2c</code>):{' '}
      <code>carousel/Carousel.kt</code> (<code>CarouselDefaults</code> L813–825: small items
      40–56dp, item spacing and content padding 0dp L819 / L822), <code>Arrangement.kt</code>,{' '}
      <code>Keylines.kt</code>, <code>KeylineList.kt</code>, <code>Strategy.kt</code>,{' '}
      <code>KeylineSnapPosition.kt</code>, <code>CarouselState.kt</code>{' '}
      (<code>animateScrollToItem</code>'s <code>spring()</code>, L101),{' '}
      <code>CarouselItemScope.kt</code>, <code>CarouselSamples.kt</code> (the extra-large mask L130;
      8dp between items and 16dp at the ends, L119–120) and the androidHostTest suites the keyline
      math is checked against; animation-core <code>AnimationSpec.kt</code> and{' '}
      <code>VectorizedAnimationSpec.kt</code>. There is no <code>CarouselTokens.kt</code>: the
      values are generated into <code>components/carousel-defaults.css</code> (lines in{' '}
      <code>PARITY.md</code>).
    </p>
    <p>
      m3.material.io Carousel (Specs, Guidelines, Accessibility; token DB{' '}
      <code>TOKEN_TABLE.43a124d2adc8a2ef</code>, <code>md.comp.carousel-item</code>: the item mask
      and state layer) for the full-screen layout and reduced motion. SOURCES register #53, #82
      (Compose's 0dp defaults; the docs use the samples' 8 / 16dp, DECISIONS D19 (19)), #83 (no
      corner radius full screen, D19 (20)) and #84 (D19 (21)).
    </p>
  </Sources>
</Base>

<script>
  import '@kyralabs/m3exp-web/elements';
</script>
